// colour names, keeping a steady beat, line names and directions, melodic and non-melodic sounds, letter and numeral patterns, the
// rules of Kenyan singing games, the message of action songs, loud and high, water at home), the teaching pack and the practical
// outcomes each knowledge skill supports (marked by the teacher with the KICD rubric, never a phone question).
// Below Grade 1 there is no HOREB map, so prerequisites name pre-primary readiness skills defined here (READINESS, written to
// g1.json under readiness as CREA.PP2.READINESS.*, for a teacher to confirm against the PP1-PP2 Creative Activities design; not rows
// of curriculum_skills), the Maths readiness skills of mathematics/g1.json (MATH.PP2.READINESS.*), Grade 1 Maths skills and Grade 1
// Environmental Activities outcomes. Merged by scripts/build-creativeactivities.mjs 1. Draft until a CBC Creative Activities teacher
// reviews it. Every question is read aloud to a Grade 1 child, with pictures described in words.
// A skill: [sub-strand key after 'CREA.G1.', id, name, outcome letters, mastery].
